```

Use the regular Composite API — not Composite Graph, whose execution order is dependency-driven and could insert the unlinked `Service_Request__c` before the `Asset`. Regular Composite executes subrequests sequentially, and `allOrNone: true` rolls back the whole call on any failure.

```http
POST /services/data/v59.0/composite HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "allOrNone": true,
  "compositeRequest": [
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v59.0/sobjects/Account",
      "referenceId": "newAccount",
      "body": {
        "Name": "Hollis Outdoor Supply"
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v59.0/sobjects/Asset",
      "referenceId": "newAsset",
      "body": {
        "Name": "Trailhead Kiosk 3000",
        "SerialNumber": "SN-88213",
        "AccountId": "@{newAccount.id}"
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v59.0/sobjects/Service_Request__c",
      "referenceId": "newRequest",
      "body": {
        "Subject__c": "Installation",
        "Serial_Number__c": "SN-88213"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

This is achieved with a single upsert by External ID, referencing the parent via its External ID:

```http
PATCH /services/data/v62.0/sobjects/Account/ERP_Customer_Id__c/ERP-10042 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "Name": "Hollis Outdoor Supply",
  "Phone": "+1 503 555 0199",
  "BillingCity": "Portland",
  "Parent": {
    "ERP_Customer_Id__c": "ERP-10000"
  }
}
